WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:29.880
One evening this spring, as part of a student-run lecture series, two man-vide

00:29.880 --> 00:35.160
for the souls of students who packed MIT's Cresky Auditorium. They were Dr. Timothy Leary,

00:35.160 --> 00:40.760
founder of the League for Spiritual Discovery, which advocates LSD as a religious sacrament,

00:40.760 --> 00:46.160
and MIT professor Jerome Letvin, who thinks of Dr. Leary as an agent of the devil. Timothy

00:46.160 --> 00:51.440
Leary began experiments with LSD as a lecturer in psychology at Harvard, Harvard dismissed

00:51.440 --> 00:58.440
him in 1963. He is now out on a $30,000 bond for possession of marijuana. Dr. Leary spoke

00:58.440 --> 01:02.840
first, mainly in darkness, while psychedelic effects were projected on the screen behind

01:02.840 --> 01:08.160
him. We have recreated these effects in color.

01:08.160 --> 01:22.080
I am beginning tonight's ceremony by offering this chalice, which I am drinking to all

01:22.080 --> 01:34.920
of us. The chalice contains a powerful and dangerous chemical given to me by the Boston

01:34.920 --> 01:50.600
water supply. It's odorless, colorless, tasteless. It's addictive. As a matter of fact,

01:50.600 --> 02:01.280
if you get hooked on it and they take it away from you, you crawl in your hands and knees,

02:01.280 --> 02:10.600
and your tongue gets black, and your eyes bow. It's also a dangerous chemical. You have

02:10.600 --> 02:14.400
to know how to use it, too much of it in wrong place, like in your lungs, and will kill

02:14.400 --> 02:25.040
you. Ten feet of it coming over your rowboat. Maybe we should pass a law against it because

02:25.040 --> 02:30.800
it's so dangerous and so addictive. Maybe only scientists should be allowed to play

02:30.800 --> 02:37.880
with it. Or maybe we could learn how to teach our kids how to use it, in which case they'll

02:37.880 --> 02:46.120
discover that water has many uses, and indeed has been used for thousands of years, for

02:46.120 --> 02:54.480
billions of years, as a way of life. It's also been used for thousands of years as a

02:54.480 --> 03:02.040
sacrament. Now you know what a sacrament is. A sacrament is a psychedelic technique. It's

03:02.040 --> 03:06.760
something that you're used to get high. Get high? Yes. A sacrament is something that gets

03:06.760 --> 03:15.640
you high. It gets you off the television stage set. Pretty solid here. Amazing how solid

03:15.640 --> 03:26.320
they make these sets these days. It gets you off the fake prop television stage set of MIT

03:26.320 --> 03:31.880
Cambridge Massachusetts United States America, and reminds you that you're not just a college

03:31.880 --> 03:41.120
student. You're not just 22 or 23 or 24 years old. You're two billion years old. Had you

03:41.120 --> 03:49.120
forgotten that? In fact, water can remind you where you came from. Remember you spent nine months

03:49.120 --> 03:56.240
in a watery medium. First nine months, this trip on this planet. Remember all that sloshing?

03:56.240 --> 04:11.520
Now, could we have the lights out now, please? I opened my ceremony. Could I have all the lights out, please?

04:11.520 --> 04:35.000
You're going to see on the screen, home movies, and slide projections of little travels and

04:35.000 --> 04:45.800
trips that we take. The slides give you the LSD experience from the inside and the movies present

04:47.800 --> 04:56.680
the observers view of an LSD trip from the outside. The movies are unedited film that's been shot

04:56.680 --> 04:59.960
minute after minute hour after hour during LSD.

